Shoshanna loves doing ballet and  gymnastics at 3:00 she's full of energy  but with parks closed and classes  canceled because of coronavirus she's  finding new ways to keep active the  corona virus pandemic has led to a big  upsurge in online fitness classes for  all ages from yoga and dance to a high  intensity cardio workout and football  it's all out there some people are even  managing to run marathons inside here in  the UK all gyms and leisure centres have  closed their doors and some parks are  off-limits because of the risk of  transmitting the virus restrictions mean  that people are being urged by Britain's  government to exercise just once a day  and only with members of your own  household for many people Fitness is  part of their daily or weekly life and  under normal circumstances this place is  full of golfers of all different ages  and abilities but they can't play at the  moment  Steve McGinty is a retired PE teacher  who plays golf and swims regularly and  if you give up and say oh I can't really  be bothered to do my exercise program  today then you're definitely feeling at  the end of the day you feel that you  have not achieved anything and therefore  in some ways ironically that kind of  Spurs you want to do more the next day  many of us are changing our lives  significantly during this crisis to stay  safe and trying to stay fit is a  challenge but doctors say it could also  help protect us now and in the future I  think it's really important to take  advantage of any opportunities that you  do have to exercise whether you know  you're allowed to go outside for walk  really taking advantage of that and also  utilizing some of the videos that might  be available online or things that you  might be able to do in the home with  yourself your family members your kids  maybe teaming up with some friends over  the Internet and you know really holding  each other to account to trying to get  in some of that physical exercise every  day not only is that going to be good  for your physical health it's also going  to be good for your mental health some  people are using this time to try out  new ways of keeping fear  none of us know how long this crisis  will last or how long will be asked to  alter our lives  Emma Haywood al Jazeera Lincolnshire
 

